# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-22 — kept for reference only, NOT installed (absent from INSTANCES).
# Per-card instances are not usable on this board: only PUMP_FAN1 drives pin 4, and it is
# taken by the hub that feeds BOTH blowers, so there is no second controllable channel.
# The live config is gpu-fan-control-hub.env (one instance, both cards, pwm2). Revisit
# these only if a SYS_FAN header ever becomes PWM-capable (needs BIOS access).
#
# Config for gpu-fan-control@gpu2 (installs to /etc/gpu-fan-control-gpu2.env).
# The PCIe-3 (chipset-slot) V620 — CT 123 `gpu2` — cooled by its own 9733 blower on
# the SYS_FAN1 header (nct6687 pwm3/fan3), via an EN-Labs PWMHUB10SMG.
#
# ⚠️ STAGED, NOT INSTALLED. `gpu2` is absent from INSTANCES in install.sh because
# pwm3 controls nothing. Add it back only after a sweep shows the fan responding.
#
# ⚠️ THE FAULT IS THE pwm3 PATH, NOT A FAN. Proven by A/B swap 2026-08-22:
#   - GPU 1's blower on PUMP_FAN1/pwm2  -> CONTROLLED (255->4301, 128->3100, 32->1046, 0->0 RPM)
#   - GPU 2's blower on SYS_FAN1/pwm3   -> 5128 RPM FLAT at every duty including 0
# Both blowers are therefore good, and the fault stayed with the header/hub when the
# fans were exchanged. Four configurations have now failed on pwm3 (fan direct, fan
# with a replacement cable, GPU1 fan via hub, GPU2 fan via hub) while pwm1/2/5/6 all
# physically drive fans on demand. Candidates, in order:
#   1. The hub's 4-pin control lead is not seated in SYS_FAN1 (per EN-Labs' own docs
#      the hub free-runs at 100% and passes no PWM if that lead is missing — which is
#      exactly the observed behaviour).
#   2. SYS_FAN1's PWM output pin is dead. Note the evidence that this header once
#      worked is historical (the NF-F12 shroud's measured ~47% stall / ~43%
#      cold-start thresholds); nothing has been PWM-controlled on pwm3 since.
#   3. The hub does not pass PWM at all (faulty unit).
# NEXT TEST: move the hub's control lead to a header PROVEN to drive a fan (pwm5 or
# pwm6 — both physically stopped case fans on 2026-08-22) and sweep that channel.
# Responds => SYS_FAN1's pin 4 is dead, so keep the hub on the working header and set
# FAN_PWM_CHANNEL to it. Still dead => the hub is faulty; return it.
#
# Until then pwm3 is pinned to 255 and this card runs at 100% fan. That is the better
# of the two possible arrangements: GPU 2 is the card that trips the watchdog (three
# times on 2026-08-15) and climbs ~33C -> 101C in ~70s on a cold long-context prefill,
# so permanent maximum airflow suits it, while the cooler ops card keeps a quiet curve.
#
# systemd EnvironmentFile= does NOT strip trailing inline comments — keep comments
# on their own lines, never after a VAR=value.

FAN_LABEL=gpu2
GPU_PCI_ADDRESS=0000:06:00.0
# SYS_FAN1 = pwm3/fan3.
FAN_PWM_CHANNEL=3

# Deliberately more aggressive than the gpu1 profile, for the reasons above.
# Re-verify that the 12% floor cold-starts this fan once it is controllable.
EDGE_MIN_C=35
EDGE_MAX_C=75
PWM_MIN_PCT=12
MIN_PWM_RAW=32
HOTSPOT_TEMP_LABELS=junction mem
HOTSPOT_OVERRIDE_C=85
HOTSPOT_RESUME_C=82

FAN_RPM_MONITOR=auto
FAN_MIN_RPM=150
FAN_FAIL_ACTION=warn
